v0.090: send DPD deliveryDescription, customsValue and currency for customs shipments

- outboundConsignment.deliveryDescription is mandatory for every non-UK
  destination and describes the consignment's contents as a whole, separate
  from the per-product descriptions inside parcels[].products[]. Sourced
  from a new editable Settings > DPD goods description (max 45 chars),
  since DPD warn vague descriptions get parcels delayed or returned.
- customsValue now sent, computed from the order lines (goods only, ex-VAT
  and ex-shipping). DPD return parcels when it is zero, so booking is now
  blocked with a clear message if the lines carry no prices.
- currency now declared explicitly (Settings, defaults GBP) rather than
  relying on the myDPD account default.
- Extended liability deliberately left off - it is a chargeable insurance
  option, not something to enable silently.

